course: dictionary
lesson: 2265
title: Create: make it new or make it happen
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To create something is to make something new that did not exist before, such as a picture, a story or a model. The word can also mean to cause something to happen, such as a feeling, a problem or a mess. «France created the metric system in the 1790s» means France made a new system of measuring that had never existed before.
explain: Look at the words around create to find its meaning. «Being chilly with wet hair doesn't create a virus.» A virus is not made by being cold, so create here means cause something to appear. The sentence still makes sense if you swap in cause, so you know you have the right meaning.
explain: The word changes its ending: create, creates, created, creating. Today you create, yesterday you created, and tomorrow you will create again. Notice that «created» tells you the action happened in the past.
fact: Create means to make something new, or to cause something to happen.
fact: The verb changes: create, creates, created, creating.
fact: Common phrases with create are «create a story», «create a mess», «create problems» and «create space».
fact: In science you might create a circuit or create a fair test. In everyday life you might create a password.
fact: Colds are caused by viruses caught from other people, and «wet hair and cold weather do not create cold viruses».
exercise: «France created the metric system in the 1790s.» What does created mean here? | *Made something new that did not exist before | Broke something old | Found something by chance | Looked at something carefully
exercise: «Being chilly with wet hair doesn't create a virus.» What does create mean here? | Wash something out | *Cause something to happen | Make a picture | Get rid of something
exercise: Which word is the past tense of create? | creating | creates | *created | create
test: Mum says, «Please do not create a mess in the kitchen.» What does create a mess mean? | *Cause a mess to happen | Hide a mess | Clean up a mess | Find a mess
test: Ella wants to create space on her desk for her model. What does create space mean? | Wait quietly | Cause a fight | *Make room | Throw things away
exam: What does create mean in «Wet hair and cold weather do not create cold viruses»? | *Cause something to happen | Stop working | Make a noise | Wash clean
